    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. Can you give me some specific examples of foods that fall into each category? Like, what are some common high-GI things they should watch out for, and what are some good low-GI swaps they could make instead?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For high-GI foods, watch out for white bread, sugary cereals, and white rice, as they cause quick sugar spikes. Good low-GI swaps include choosing whole-grain bread, brown rice, and quinoa instead. On the fruit side, opt for apples or berries over sugary juices. Incorporating more legumes and non-starchy vegetables is also a powerful way to keep meals low-GI.",
      "source": "target",
