    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that's a good list. One more thing—some clients get overwhelmed by the idea of \"restriction.\" Is there a way to explain the physiological \"why\" behind the spikes in a way that's more memorable or illustrative? Like, how does the body actually react to those sudden surges compared to the gradual ones?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Think of their body's insulin like a traffic controller; a sudden flood of sugar from high-GI food overwhelms the system, forcing the controller to work overtime to manage the sudden rush. Gradual, low-GI food releases sugar slowly, allowing the insulin controller to manage the flow smoothly and efficiently. This prevents the intense, sharp demands on their pancreas that sudden sugar surges create. It's less about deprivation and more about choosing foods that let their system run calmly.",
      "source": "target",
